## Context

The `--dry-run` flag already exists at every level (CLI args, RunOptions, ExecutionOptions, step executor), but the current output is poor — dry-run goes through the full spinner/execution loop, showing "✓ step_name (0ms)" which looks like the step actually ran. The "Would run: {command}" text from the executor is captured in `result.output` but never displayed. Interactive prompts still fire in dry-run mode. The user asked for dry-run to "print what would be installed or changed without actually executing."

## Approach

Add a dedicated dry-run display path in `run_with_ui` that bypasses the spinner/execution loop and instead prints a clear summary of what each step would do.

## Changes

### 1. `src/runner/workflow.rs` — `run_with_ui` method (~lines 345-825)

Add a dry-run branch inside the per-step loop (after dependency check, ~line 388), before the interactive prompts and spinner:

```
if options.dry_run {
    // Show step header: "[1/7] step_name — title"
    ui.message(&step_display);

    // Check completed_check status (informational only)
    if let Some(ref check) = step.completed_check {
        let check_result = run_check(check, project_root);
        if check_result.complete {
            ui.message("    Status: already complete (would skip without --force)")
        }
    }

    // Show command (masked if sensitive)
    let resolved_cmd = resolve_string(&step.command, context)?;
    if step.sensitive {
        ui.message("    Command: [sensitive — hidden in dry-run]");
    } else {
        ui.message(&format!("    Command: {}", resolved_cmd));
    }

    // Show before/after hooks
    for hook in &step.before {
        let resolved = resolve_string(hook, context)?;
        ui.message(&format!("    Before: {}", resolved));
    }
    for hook in &step.after {
        let resolved = resolve_string(hook, context)?;
        ui.message(&format!("    After: {}", resolved));
    }

    // Record as success with no duration
    results.push(StepResult::success(&step.name, Duration::ZERO, None, Some(format!("Would run: {}", resolved_cmd))));
    ui.show_workflow_progress(index + 1, total, start.elapsed());
    continue;
}
```

